-- title:
--   Flatness from flatness modulo all powers of I
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings with $B$ an $A$-algebra, both $A$ and $B$ Noetherian, and let $I$ be an ideal of $A$. Assume that the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $I$ under the structure map $A \to B$ is contained in the Jacobson radical of $B$, i.e. in the Jacobson radical of the zero ideal, the intersection of all maximal ideals of $B$. Assume further that for every natural number $n$ the $A/I^n$-module $(A/I^n) \otimes_A B$ — the base change of $B$ along $A \to A/I^n$, i.e. $B/I^nB$ — is flat over $A/I^n$. Then $B$ is flat as an $A$-module. (The case $n = 0$ of the hypothesis is vacuous, both rings being zero; the content lies in $n \ge 1$.) No local hypothesis is imposed on $A$ or $B$: the containment of $IB$ in the Jacobson radical of $B$ replaces the usual requirement that $A \to B$ be a local homomorphism of local rings with $I = \mathfrak{m}_A$.
--
--   This is the local criterion of flatness in the form where the Jacobson radical condition replaces locality, as in Bourbaki and EGA $0_{\mathrm{III}}$. It is used to establish flatness of a proper morphism from flatness of its pullbacks along $\operatorname{Spec}(A/\mathfrak{m}^n) \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.flat_of_forall_flat_pullback_snd_specMap_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_of_isProper`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.flat_of_forall_flat_pullback_snd_specMap_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_of_isProper).
